  "today": "Before the month-end NYMEX invoice run, Gas Settlements (Rebecca Ford's group; Beatrice Reyna does the asking) calls or emails Reporting and the regional risk leads to ask whether any book codes are new or have just started holding third-party financial deals. Settlements needs a list of whom to ask from William Kelly (East, Central, West, Texas leads), and the list goes out of date when people leave: in October Reyna had to ask who replaced Kyle Etter, and Jeff Gossett forwarded her question on to Kelly and Darron Giron. The check depends on memory and on asking the right people: in August Settlements found at least 4 such books on its own that nobody had told them about.",
