{
  "name": "Seven Oaks meter 6884 monthly plant adjustment deals",
  "today": "Each month the plant operator at Seven Oaks (Teco, later PG&E and then El Paso) makes an adjustment at meter 986884. Depending on the month, this makes HPL a buyer or a seller. The arrangement was never written up as a contract, and the Sitara purchase and sale deals at the meter keep expiring or ending up under the wrong counterparty. When the allocation arrives with no deal to match it, Volume Management or Settlements cannot draft the volume. They park it on strangers gas and email logistics and the trader for deal numbers or extensions. This happened for May 2000, December 2000, and January, February, April and May 2001. In February 2001 the extension was blocked on the last day changes could be made, because Teco had been suspended as a counterparty.",
  "change": "Set up standing (evergreen) purchase and sale deals with El Paso at meter 986884 so each month's adjustment can be drafted without asking anyone for a deal.",
  "explanation": "Logistics and the trader (Daren Farmer) set up one evergreen purchase deal and one evergreen sale deal with El Paso, Teco's successor, at meter 986884. Both are priced the way the adjustment is settled today. Contracts, with George Weissman, would also write up the buy/sell arrangement, which runs for the remaining lease term, if they judge it safe to do so. In March 2000 Weissman was reluctant to raise it with Teco while other contracts were coming up for renewal, so the standing deals alone would still remove most of the chasing. Afterwards, Volume Management and Settlements allocate and draft each month's adjustment against the standing deal that matches its direction. They contact the trader only if a volume looks unusual or the counterparty changes again.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/1626.eml",
      "quote": "I need to have the purchase from (Teco) and sale to \n(Teco) deals in order to allocate correctly.  For May 00, we are purchasing \nfrom Teco.  I am allocating this to strangers gas at \n  moment"
    },
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/2099.eml",
      "quote": "Do we have the buy/Sell deal for El Paso ( formerly Teco)  for January 01 \nProd?"
    },
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/2150.eml",
      "quote": "This deal has expired for Teco Gas Processing, but we did have a sale in \n02/01.\nShould this deal be extended?"
    },
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/95.eml",
      "quote": "I need to have deal 637225 extended to include April and May 2001.  The allocations we received from El Paso show that HPLC sold gas to them at meter 6884 for both months."
    },
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/2067.eml",
      "quote": "I do not show a sale in the system at the meter"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/1626.eml",
      "quote": "This adjustment arrangement doesn't seem to be \npapered - it's just occurred each month for the past 5 years on a relatively \nroutine basis.",
      "note": "The adjustment happens every month and has no contract behind it, which is why the deals keep going missing."
    },
    {
      "file": "farmer-d/logistics/1626.eml",
      "quote": "Since the adjustment arrangement isn't papered, we've been having difficulty \nproperly reflecting the deal in sitara and unify.",
